===Etymology===
Composed of [[Ekavian]] Serbo-Croatian {{term|sc=Cyrl|бео|бе̏о|white|lang=sh}} (< {{proto|Slavic|bělъ|lang=sh}}) and {{term|sc=Cyrl|град|гра̑д|city|lang=sh}} (< {{proto|Slavic|gordъ|lang=sh}}). The city is named after the white wall of the fortress that enclosed the city. See also {{term|sc=Cyrl|Биоград|lang=sh}}, {{term|Белгород|Бе́лгород|tr=Bélgorod|sc=Cyrl|lang=ru}}, {{term|Białogard}}.

